WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.750
I am aware that I inhale, I am aware that I exhale, I am my breath,

2
00:00:05.750 --> 00:00:10.390
I become aware of my body, I relax my body, I generate

3
00:00:10.390 --> 00:00:14.810
a feeling of joy, I generate a feeling of happiness in the present.

4
00:00:17.500 --> 00:00:22.370
I become aware of my pain, I embrace my pain, I take care of it.

5
00:00:22.900 --> 00:00:26.900
It is important to have good motivation when you start to meditate.

6
00:00:28.067 --> 00:00:30.077
will present you with obstacles.

7
00:00:30.077 --> 00:00:33.227
The first obstacle you will encounter is laziness.

8
00:00:33.227 --> 00:00:37.577
It will bring you a second subtlety, which is called active laziness.

9
00:00:37.577 --> 00:00:38.403
I was doing a

10
00:00:40.007 --> 00:00:42.617
lot of things except going to meditate.

11
00:00:42.617 --> 00:00:46.367
A third form of laziness that still arises is abandonment.

12
00:00:46.367 --> 00:00:50.207
But then you tell yourself no, ultimately it's not for me.

13
00:00:50.207 --> 00:00:51.007
The antidote

14
00:00:52.207 --> 00:00:54.221
is to find a proper motivation.

15
00:00:54.467 --> 00:00:58.588
This motivation must be not only for yourself, but also for others.

16
00:00:58.915 --> 00:01:03.155
The second real obstacle you will encounter, is that when you learn to meditate,

17
00:01:03.155 --> 00:01:05.820
initially, there is a methodology in learning.

18
00:01:07.315 --> 00:01:11.415
The obstacle you will encounter is the complete forgetting of what needs to be done.

19
00:01:11.415 --> 00:01:15.295
At one point, I was meditating, or rather, I thought I was meditating,

20
00:01:15.295 --> 00:01:18.543
I was sitting there, ultimately, I was quite lost in thought.

21
00:01:18.795 --> 00:01:21.693
I understood that meditation is a training of the mind.

22
00:01:21.693 --> 00:01:24.587
It comes from a very ancient etymology which means...

23
00:01:24.863 --> 00:01:27.567
Truly learning to discover one's own functioning.

24
00:01:27.803 --> 00:01:30.634
You are not always well when you meditate, but that's okay.

25
00:01:30.634 --> 00:01:33.093
I learn to recognize, to train my mind.

26
00:01:33.203 --> 00:01:37.273
And the antidote, which I think is very interesting for us in the practice of

27
00:01:37.273 --> 00:01:39.455
meditation, is attention, is mindfulness.

28
00:01:39.703 --> 00:01:43.793
To discover this energy that is in your mind, this energy which is concentration,

29
00:01:43.793 --> 00:01:46.323
and which will gradually open you to another energy,

30
00:01:46.323 --> 00:01:48.223
which is the profound vision of things.

31
00:01:48.223 --> 00:01:49.775
But one must proceed gradually.

32
00:01:49.775 --> 00:01:52.345
It's like when you enter a space where on the walls.

33
00:01:52.345 --> 00:01:54.320
There are secrets that can be unveiled.

34
00:01:54.470 --> 00:01:57.115
I enter with a candle, and the candle is your mind.

35
00:01:57.250 --> 00:02:01.703
Initially, the candle flickers like this, meaning there isn't much luminosity.

36
00:02:01.770 --> 00:02:05.740
But if, through the foundational practice of your meditation,

37
00:02:05.740 --> 00:02:10.430
you learn to completely stabilize the flame, a kind of luminous halo appears,

38
00:02:10.430 --> 00:02:11.994
a clarity that emerges.

39
00:02:12.890 --> 00:02:14.850
Well, it's somewhat the same thing.

40
00:02:14.850 --> 00:02:19.560
If you truly manage to stabilize your mind, suddenly you will perceive a kind of

41
00:02:19.560 --> 00:02:20.315
luminous clarity.

42
00:02:20.338 --> 00:02:22.118
that appears in one's mind.

43
00:02:22.118 --> 00:02:25.128
This clarity leads you to profound insight.

44
00:02:25.128 --> 00:02:29.518
One must learn to stabilize the mind because it is an entire process of

45
00:02:29.518 --> 00:02:30.598
stabilization.

46
00:02:30.598 --> 00:02:32.256
Therefore, it is learning

47
00:02:32.256 --> 00:02:37.356
to develop this clarity of mind primarily through the energy of mindfulness,

48
00:02:37.938 --> 00:02:41.778
concentration, and the energy of profound insight.

49
00:02:43.998 --> 00:02:47.378
One must practice. Everyone can access this.

